# ── WEIGHTS AND RUN ARTIFACTS ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⛔ Each adapter_model.safetensors is 308 MB and every checkpoint carries an
# optimizer.pt beside it. GitHub HARD-REJECTS any file over 100 MB, and a large
# blob committed even once stays in the history forever — the repair is a history
# rewrite, so this file has to exist before the first commit, not after.
#
# Nothing of scientific value is lost: the ledger, the logs and the measured
# numbers ARE committed (runs/act2/*/logs, *.jsonl below), and the adapters are
# reproducible from the corpus builder plus the pinned training command in
# docs/RUNBOOK_ACT2_PILOT.md.
runs/act2/tlon_run*/adapter/
runs/act2/adapter/
**/checkpoint-*/
*.safetensors
*.bin
optimizer.pt
scheduler.pt

# ── THE CORPUS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⭐ 80,000 rows / ~36 MB, and FULLY REGENERABLE:
#     python tools/act2_build_corpus.py --n 40000
# Deterministic at seed 20620 against the frozen lexicon, so the builder plus the
# recorded sha256 is a stronger artifact than the file — anyone can rebuild it
# and check they got the identical bytes.
runs/act2/corpus/*.jsonl
# same convention for the multi-turn corpus: the rows are
# reproducible from act2_build_multiturn.py + the manifest,
# which IS committed (it carries the provocation sha, the
# force map, the design zeros, and the held-variable record).
runs/act2/corpus_mt/*.jsonl
# and the ki-target probe's two corpora — 27 MB each, seed-pinned and
# sha-pinned in tools/pipeline_ki_target.sh, so they rebuild byte-identical.
runs/act2/ki_target/corpus_*/*.jsonl
# same for the recipe-variance seeds — sha-pinned in the pipeline
runs/act2/recipe_var/corpus_*/*.jsonl

# ── PYTHON ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── LOCAL / EDITOR ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ── KEPT ON PURPOSE (documenting the exceptions, so they are not "missed") ──
# !runs/act2/**/logs/          the measured output of every run
# !runs/act2/**/ledger.jsonl   the spend + result ledger
# !runs/act2/corpus/meta.json  the exposure report the corpus was built to

# ── COST LEDGERS — NOT PUBLIC ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spend accounting is Nate's, not the research record. The ledgers stay on the
# machine; nothing about a result depends on what it cost.
**/ledger_tlon.jsonl
**/ledger_harden.jsonl
runs/act2/ledger.jsonl
